      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express it in the form \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\), where \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers that multiply to 2008 and add up to \\( b \\). The quadratic equation \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) can be factorized as:\n\\[ x^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q). \\]\nBy expanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\\[ x^2 + bx + 2008 = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq. \\]\nThis gives us the relationships \\( b = p + q \\) and \\( pq = 2008 \\). To find the smallest positive \\( b \\), we need to find the unique pairs \\( (p, q) \\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\) and \\( p + q \\) is minimized. This can be done by considering the factors of 2008. The factors of 2008 are:\n\\[ \\pm 1, \\pm 2, \\pm 4, \\pm 8, \\pm 251, \\pm 502, \\pm 1004, \\pm 2008. \\]\nThe pairs \\((p, q)\\) that multiply to 2008 and minimize \\( p + q \\) are \\((1, 2008)\\) and \\((-1, -2008)\\), \\((2, 1004)\\) and \\((-2, -1004)\\), \\((4, 502)\\) and \\((-4, -502)\\), \\((8, 251)\\) and \\((-8, -251)\\).\n\nNow we compute the sums of these pairs:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n1 + 2008 &= 2009, \\\\\n-1 + (-2008) &= -2009, \\\\\n2 + 1004 &= 1006, \\\\\n-2 + (-1004) &= -1006, \\\\\n4 + 502 &= 506, \\\\\n-4 + (-502) &= -506, \\\\\n8 + 251 &= 259, \\\\\n-8 + (-251) &= -259.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nAmong these, the smallest positive sum is 2009. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2009} \\]\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function to find the smallest positive b\ndef find_smallest_b(n):\n    # Factors of n\n    factors = []\n    for i in range(1, abs(n) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            factors.append(i)\n            factors.append(-i)\n    \n    # Find the smallest positive b\n    min_b = float('inf')\n    for f1 in factors:\n        for f2 in factors:\n            if n % (f1 * f2) == 0:\n                b = f1 + f2\n                if b > 0 and b < min_b:\n                    min_b = b\n    return min_b\n\n# Given value of n\nn = 2008\n# Find the smallest positive b\nsmallest_b = find_smallest_b(n)\nprint(smallest_b)\n```",
